  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote the reef scene in `src/main.ts`. `typecheck` passes. I could not run the app or `vite build`, so none of it has been checked in a browser.\n\n- **Seabed:** a custom GLSL sand grid with rippled geometry. Its shader adds two layers of drifting caustics, red-absorbing depth tint and fade to the fog colour.\n- **Corals:** five branching corals, three brain corals, three tube clusters, three fan corals with translucent webbing, and 40 rocks.\n- **Plants:** 80 seaweed strands and 7 anemones with tentacles, all swaying each frame.\n- **Fish:**\n  - Two schools of 22 and 18 small fish (40 in total) swim in loose groups.\n  - Three larger solitary fish follow their own elliptical paths.\n  - All fish have wagging tails and dorsal fins.\n- **Light and water:** a teal background with exponential fog, a hemisphere light and a shadow-casting sun with a slight flicker. Faint translucent sun shafts add to the look.\n- **Bubbles:** 84 instanced bubbles rise from six vents. I built them from instanced spheres instead of the particle effect, because I couldn't confirm that effect draws pixels.\n- **Camera:** a slow orbit at radius 20, with a height bob and a small target bob. The orbit rig turns the camera on its own. A per-frame `app.camera?.setPose` call adds the bob, so if `app.camera` is missing the orbit still works but the bob doesn't.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set two animation frames after `app.ready()`.\n\nI'm least sure of two things. The translucent shafts and fan webbing depend on `opacity` being honored by `material.pbr`. The per-frame fish, plant and bubble motion depends on `setInstanceMatrices`, which I read from the engine source but did not run.\n\n",
